# JXP Documentation

This project is built on [JXP](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/) (`jxp` ^2.15). Source and local development: [WorkSpaceMan/jxp](https://github.com/WorkSpaceMan/jxp) at `../jxp` when using `npm run link:jxp` (see `jxp-development` rule). Before implementing or changing JXP-related behavior, **consult @JXP** and follow its patterns instead of guessing from Mongoose or Express conventions alone.

## When to consult @JXP

Always look up @JXP before work on:

- Schemas (`JXPSchema`, field types, validation, `perms`)
- Links (`link`, `map_to`, populate/query params)
- REST API behavior (filtering, searching, pagination, field selection)
- Hooks (`pre`/`post` on schemas; `pre_hooks`/`callbacks` in `bin/server.js`)
- Roles, permissions, and groups
- Stored procedures, aggregations, bulk writes, and advanced queries
- Authentication, tokens, and refresh tokens

## Project conventions

- Models live in `models/*_model.js` and register with `JXPSchema.model(...)`.
- `JXPSchema`, `ObjectId`, and `Mixed` are globals — use `/* global JXPSchema */` at the top of model files.
- Server bootstrap and API hooks are in `bin/server.js`.
- Internal API calls use `jxp-helper` via `common/apihelper.js` or model-local helpers.
- Link schema names use PascalCase (`link: "User"`); populate query params use lowercase (`?populate[user]=name`).

## Key doc sections

- [Schemas](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/schemas/) — definitions, links, options, pre/post functions
- [RESTful API](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/) — GET/POST/PUT/DELETE, populate, filter, search
- [Roles and Permissions](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/roles/)
- [Hooks](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/hooks/)
- [Aggregations](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/aggregations/) and [Queries](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/queries/)

If @JXP and existing project code disagree, prefer @JXP unless there is a documented project-specific reason not to.
